# Merge Conflicts

A merge conflict can occur when different branches make incompatible changes to the same part of a file.

### How to Handle a Merge Conflict

1. Identify the conflicting file(s).
2. Open the file and review the changes.
3. Decide which changes should be retained.
4. Remove the conflict markers and unwanted changes.
5. Save the corrected file.
6. Stage the file.
7. Commit the resolution.

```bash
git add <conflicted_file>
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict"
```

### DevOps Perspective

> The best approach is not only to fix merge conflicts, but to prevent unnecessary conflicts through good branching, communication, and frequent synchronization.

