## Git Rebase

`git rebase` moves or reapplies commits onto a new base commit.

It is commonly used to maintain a cleaner, more linear history.

Example:

```text
master:
cm1 → cm2 → f1cm1 → f1cm2 → f1cm3
```

Suppose `feature2` was created from `cm2`:

```text
feature2:
cm1 → cm2 → f2cm1 → f2cm2 → f2cm3
```

Rebase feature2:

```bash
git switch feature2
git rebase master
```

Conceptually:

```text
cm1 → cm2 → f1cm1 → f1cm2 → f1cm3 → f2cm1 → f2cm2 → f2cm3
```

Then:

```bash
git switch master
git merge feature2
```

> Rebase rewrites commit history. Avoid rebasing commits that have already been shared if doing so would disrupt other developers.

