# Git Squash

Squashing combines multiple commits into a smaller number of commits, often one logical commit.

Example:

```text
feature1:

cm1 → cm2 → f1cm1 → f1cm2 → f1cm3 → f1cm4 → f1cm5
```

From the target branch:

```bash
git switch master
git merge --squash feature1
git commit -m "Combined changes from feature1"
```

The feature changes are combined into a single new commit on the target branch.

